6165ea6aee 2026-10-20
Create a project's folder on its first save; remove the recovery mirror

Every blank project JusPrin opened got a folder under jusprin/projects at
once, and nothing removed it when nothing was ever saved. Each launch
left two (the shell's first project and Orca's startup new project), and
each blank New Project one more; 147 had built up on one machine.

ProjectVersionStore now creates the folder, and takes the project lock,
on the first write (pending metadata, the project document, or a chat
restore). That write refuses if another instance saved the same project
identity after this store opened. A project whose folder already exists
opens as before. Home's project list treats a missing projects folder as
no projects yet, as the two other readers of that folder already did.

The per-project recovery mirror under jusprin/recovery is removed. In
managed mode it was never written, only read once as an older copy of
the chat state when a project was adopted; its newest files date from
2026-09-29.

Tests: the shell harness checks that a fresh start and a restart leave
no unsaved folder (both failed before the change), and the workspace
harness checks the store's first-write behaviour. Workspace harness,
the --autosave-seed/--autosave-reopen pair, the default shell harness
and agent_bridge_tests all pass.

