The Phase 1 JusPrin production shell (built 2026-08-29 on worktree branch
claude/agent-webview-bridge-phase-1-bd0c05) deliberately diverges from the
POC's FullWindowUiSpike: it keeps MainFrame's Notebook, its pages, and its
selection flow intact, hides only the tab strip (`GetBtnsListCtrl()->Hide()`
— wxBookCtrlBase gives a hidden controller zero size so pages fill the area),
and re-sizers the Notebook next to fork-owned StatusRow/AgentPane panels.
Slice reuses the stock dispatch (post `EVT_GLTOOLBAR_SLICE_PLATE` +
`SetSelection(tpPreview)`), so every `GetSelection()`-based predicate and the
stock Prepare/Preview flow keep working. Upstream seams: one attach call in
the MainFrame ctor and a neutral `Plater::set_sidebar_available` policy guard
in `priv::enable_sidebar` (needed because select_view_3D/new_project/
load_project re-enable the sidebar). Both seam sites had 0 upstream commits
since fork base 8500fcdcca. Evidence and gaps:
[[agent-docs/jusprin/production-shell-phase-1.md]] in the repo.
--- architecture
| Dropped on Home | Same | Same |
| Home's **Open…** button, File › Open Project (Cmd+O) | Same | Same |
| Dropped on the Prepare canvas | Added to the open project | New project, as above. OrcaSlicer's "open as project or import geometry?" question is not asked |
| **+ Add model** in the Plates and Project pane, File › Import (Cmd+I) | Added to the open project | Its geometry is added to the open project, without its settings (OrcaSlicer's Import) |
| The Agent composer's + › 3D model, a drop on the Agent pane, or a request in the chat | Attached; the agent adds it to the open project (`object_import`) | Same |

Rules that follow from the table:

- A model file never silently lands in whatever project happened to be open behind Home. Before 2026-10-24 Home's Import button did exactly that, because it called OrcaSlicer's `add_model`, and from 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-28 the most recent project reopened behind Home at startup. Home now starts with a blank project behind it, but whatever is open there is still not where a file opened from Home goes.
- A file opened from the OS lands in the running JusPrin. OrcaSlicer's default starts a second process for a .3mf; JusPrin runs as a single instance on every platform.
- Several files opened or dropped together make one new project holding all of them.
